lauren (AE): Heads-up: RiverTrust wants a short POC to migrate from CompetitorA -> Redwood. They rely on streaming chat + function calls + precise stop-token trimming. Kickoff Fri 9am PT. Need a plan for compat shim, eval parity, POC pricing, and security answers. Who can pick this up?

nate (SE): I can own the compat shim. Do we have a sample stream shape? They expect choices[0] always and partial function chunks emitted as 'func_stream'.

lauren (AE): Samples in the drive: https://redwood.internal/rivertrust/poc-samples. They also flag that some downstream consumers rely on final function call emitted after all chunks.

sam (Eng): Two migration notes: 1) Tokenization differences may increase token usage ~7-10% for their templates 1 - include a preflight token-count. 2) Stop sequence behavior: their SDK trims stop tokens - shim should strip stops exactly.

nate (SE): Plan: lightweight proxy that maps CompetitorA chat shape -> Redwood, streams deltas back as CompetitorA-style events, normalizes function args (preserve raw string vs parsed JSON based on client), and implements stop-trim shim.

nate (SE): Quick proxy sketch:
```
// proxy: /v1/compA/chat -> Redwood
app.post('/v1/compA/chat', async (req,res)=>{
  const mapped = mapCompAToRedwood(req.body);
  const r = await fetch(REDWOOD_CHAT, {method:'POST', body: JSON.stringify(mapped)});
  for await (const chunk of r.body){
    const event = parseRedwoodChunk(chunk);
    const out = mapToCompAEvent(event);
    res.write(out);
  }
});
```

anya (Security): RiverTrust asked about SOC2, VPC/private deployments, and KMS/HSM. Quick answers: SOC2 Type II available under NDA; Redwood Private supports VPC peering and on-prem; KMS integration available and HSM can be provided for Private. I'll prepare a one-pager.

mike (Pricing): POC pricing: hosted usage estimate ~$700-2200/month depending on tokens. Dedicated 30d trial lowers unit cost (~30% discount) but needs short commit. Send qps and avg tokens/session and I9ll model both hosted vs trial.

lauren (AE): RiverTrust expects peak 9 qps, avg 2 qps; typical prompts ~180-320 tokens, many function calls with 1-4KB JSON responses. I uploaded a prompt set in the drive.

sam (Eng): Function-calling gotchas we9ve hit: 1) parsed JSON vs raw string arg shapes; preserve original if downstream expects string. 2) Stream ordering: if their client needs partial function chunks then a final consolidated function_call event, buffer as needed.

nate (SE): I9ll add normalization for null vs missing fields and preserve choices[0] semantics. Will also include a stop-trim test suite.

deploy-bot: POC environment created: rivertrust-poc-2026 (env id: poc-9801). Access: AE/SE/Eng/Security.

anya (Security): Drafted sec one-pager and SOC2 reference; attaching to the drive now. If they require pen-test evidence we9ll coordinate with Legal and Infra.

mike (Pricing): Draft quote in progress. Lina on pricing ops - can you sanity-check the reserve numbers if RiverTrust wants a 30d trial?

lauren (AE): Action items: Nate = proxy + tests + repo link, Sam = eval script + token comparison, Anya = sec one-pager, Mike = POC quote. I9ll run kickoff Fri and invite RiverTrust. Tag me on regressions. :raised_hands:
